@defgroup micro-test-plus-string-operators String Operators
@brief Overloaded operators for string comparison.

@details
Operators are provided specifically for comparing string types, such as
`std::string_view`. These operators enable clear, expressive assertions
when verifying string values in test cases, supporting both equality and
inequality checks.

Using these dedicated operators ensures concise, readable tests that
accurately reflect intended logic. The framework ensures correct string
comparisons and reports failed checks with both actual and expected values
for clear diagnostics.

@par Examples

@code{.cpp}
#include <string_view>
using namespace std::literals; // For the "sv" literal.
namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;
// ...

ts.test ("Check strings with operators", [] (auto& t) {
  using namespace mt::operators;

  t.expect (std::string_view{ compute_ultimate_answer () } == "forty-two"sv)
      << "ultimate answer == 'forty-two'";
});
@endcode
